Z||000000||Loki||03-14-2001||12:01 PM||||Well decided to keep my 86Se black and go with a black and orange interior...Hope Mr.Mike is up for the challenge of orange leather   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What ya think? Good combo?<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||03-14-2001||12:32 PM||||Happy Halloween!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, interesting idea, especially considering the use of orange lighting in the Fiero. It will be interesting to see how you execute it. I think I would keep orange as an accent color. You know, shift boot, knob, piping or stitching on seats, accent on steering wheel. I think doing the dash or seats in orange would be a bit much, but you could probably get away w/ orange carpeting.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||03-14-2001||01:06 PM||||Orange would be the trim peices (radio, gauges, etc) and not the whole seat covers...But black AND orange. Not alot of orange but as you put it, as an accent...<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
