Z||000009||AusFiero||03-20-2001||05:25 PM||||Sounds like it should look good. I have just redone the interior in my red Fiero (86 GT Fastback,T-Tops) and have featured a lot of red in the interior.<P>Grey with Red piping and red inserts on the seats, red accents on a new Boss Steering wheel. Sony explode stereo featuring red speaker cones including the sub which is now mounted between the seats where the glovebox??? used to be, in a homemade console/Sub Box. Red accent panels on the doors. Have also included a lot of Carbon Fibre and am in the process now of doing the silver dash faces in carbon fibre, with white face gauges and all switches are getting changed to silver to match a bit of polished and anodised alloy I have also used.<P>Will post pictures when it is all done. Which will be soon as it is only 3 weeks or so till the Australian Pontiac Nationals where I hope to clean up the Fiero section. Shouldn't be too hard, there is only 5 Fieros going.<P>Went to the upholsterers to get a rip fixed, $4000 later...ahhhh Fieros. (c:<P>I will stop waffling on now, hope the orange works just as well.||||reg||1
